package legal

templ TermsOfService() {
	<article>
		<header>
			<h1>Terms of Service</h1>
			<p>Effective date: May 28, 2026</p>
		</header>
		<section>
			<h2>1. Service</h2>
			<p>Conex lets account holders create, manage, and publish simple websites under Conex-hosted paths. Some site management features require an account and an active session.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>2. Accounts and access</h2>
			<p>You are responsible for the email address used to access your account and for all activity that occurs through your account. Conex may send one-time verification codes to authenticate access and account changes.</p>
			<p>You agree to provide accurate account information, keep it current, and notify Conex if you believe your account has been used without authorization.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>3. User content</h2>
			<p>You keep ownership of the site names, tags, and HTML content you submit. You grant Conex permission to store, process, display, and serve that content as needed to operate the service.</p>
			<p>You must not submit content that is illegal, infringes rights, contains malware, attempts to abuse the platform, or violates another person's privacy or security.</p>
			<p>If you publish or upload personal data about another person, you are responsible for having a lawful basis, required consent, and all notices needed under applicable data protection laws, including Costa Rica Law No. 8968 and the GDPR when they apply.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>4. Published sites</h2>
			<p>Sites may be private or public depending on their stored status. Public sites can be viewed by anyone with the site URL. You are responsible for reviewing content before making a site public.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>5. Plans and availability</h2>
			<p>Conex may offer free or paid plans with different limits and renewal terms. We may change, suspend, or discontinue features when needed to maintain or improve the service.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>6. Account deletion</h2>
			<p>You may delete your account through the service. Deleting an account removes the account and its sites from active use, subject to backups, logs, legal obligations, and operational retention.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>7. Data protection requests</h2>
			<p>Conex handles personal data as described in the Privacy Policy. If you ask Conex to access, correct, delete, restrict, object to, port, or stop processing personal data, Conex will handle the request under the Privacy Policy and applicable law.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>8. Suspension and removal</h2>
			<p>Conex may suspend access to accounts or remove content when reasonably necessary to protect the service, comply with law, address security risks, respond to rights requests, or enforce these terms.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>9. Disclaimers and liability</h2>
			<p>The service is provided as is and as available. To the maximum extent allowed by law, Conex is not liable for indirect, incidental, special, consequential, or punitive damages, or for lost data, profits, or business opportunities.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>10. Changes</h2>
			<p>We may update these terms. Continued use of Conex after an update means you accept the updated terms.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>11. Contact</h2>
			<p>Questions about these terms can be sent to the operator of Conex through the support or contact channel provided for the service.</p>
		</section>
	</article>
}

templ PrivacyPolicy() {
	<article>
		<header>
			<h1>Privacy Policy</h1>
			<p>Effective date: May 28, 2026</p>
		</header>
		<section>
			<h2>1. Controller and scope</h2>
			<p>This policy explains how Conex processes personal data for its hosted website creation and account services. The controller is the operator of Conex, reachable through the support or contact channel provided for the service.</p>
			<p>Conex applies this policy in line with Costa Rica Law No. 8968 on protection of the person regarding personal data processing and, where applicable, the General Data Protection Regulation of the European Union.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>2. Information we collect</h2>
			<p>Conex collects information you provide, including your email address, site paths, site names, tags, and site HTML. The service also creates account, login, email-change, plan, subscription, and session records needed to operate account features.</p>
			<p>Responses requested by Conex are generally required when they are needed to create an account, authenticate access, provide a requested feature, process a subscription, secure the service, or comply with law. If you do not provide required information, some features may not work.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>3. Authentication information</h2>
			<p>When you log in or request an email change, Conex stores temporary verification request data and sends one-time codes by email. Access and refresh tokens are issued so clients can authenticate API requests.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>4. Usage and technical data</h2>
			<p>Conex may process request metadata such as IP address, user agent, requested URL, response status, and timestamps in server logs, security systems, and operational monitoring.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>5. Purposes and legal bases</h2>
			<p>We use information to provide accounts, authenticate users, send verification email, create and serve sites, manage subscriptions, protect the service, troubleshoot problems, and comply with legal obligations.</p>
			<p>Depending on the context, Conex processes personal data based on your informed consent, performance of the requested service or contract, compliance with legal obligations, and legitimate interests such as security, abuse prevention, service maintenance, and recordkeeping. Consent may be withdrawn in the same manner in which it was provided, without retroactive effect.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>6. Public content</h2>
			<p>Public sites are available to anyone who visits their URL and may be indexed, archived, shared, or copied by third parties. Do not publish personal or confidential information unless you intend it to be public.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>7. Recipients and service providers</h2>
			<p>We may share personal data with infrastructure, database, email, logging, hosting, payment, analytics, security, and professional service providers as needed to operate Conex. These providers may access personal data only for authorized service purposes and must protect it under appropriate confidentiality and security obligations.</p>
			<p>Conex may also disclose information when required by law, court order, competent authority, or a valid rights request, or when necessary to protect users, the service, or the public.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>8. International transfers</h2>
			<p>Conex and its providers may process personal data in Costa Rica, the United States, the European Economic Area, or other countries where service infrastructure is located. When personal data is transferred internationally, Conex uses appropriate safeguards required by applicable law, such as contractual commitments, provider security controls, consent where required, and other lawful transfer mechanisms.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>9. Sensitive data</h2>
			<p>Conex does not require you to provide sensitive personal data, such as information about health, biometrics, genetics, race or ethnic origin, political opinions, religious or philosophical beliefs, socioeconomic condition, sex life, or sexual orientation. You must not publish sensitive data about another person unless you have a lawful basis and the person's express consent or another exception allowed by law.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>10. Retention</h2>
			<p>We keep account and site information while your account exists or as needed to provide the service. Temporary verification data, tokens, backups, and logs may be retained for limited operational, security, dispute, audit, tax, accounting, or legal reasons.</p>
			<p>Conex deletes, anonymizes, or de-identifies personal data when it is no longer relevant or necessary for the purpose for which it was collected, unless a longer retention period is required or permitted by law. Personal data that may affect its holder will not be kept in identifiable form beyond the period allowed by applicable law without a lawful reason.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>11. Security and confidentiality</h2>
			<p>We use reasonable technical and organizational measures to protect information, but no internet service can guarantee absolute security.</p>
			<p>People and providers authorized to process personal data for Conex are expected to keep it confidential, including after their relationship with Conex ends, except where disclosure is legally required.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>12. Your rights</h2>
			<p>You may request access to your personal data, confirmation of whether Conex processes your personal data, information about the purposes and use of your data, correction, updating, deletion, blocking, restriction, objection, portability where applicable, and withdrawal of consent. You may also object to direct marketing and request human review where an applicable law gives you rights related to automated decision-making.</p>
			<p>Conex will respond to rights requests within the time required by applicable law. For requests governed by Costa Rica Law No. 8968, Conex will resolve access, rectification, or deletion requests within five business days after receipt, unless another legal rule applies.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>13. How to exercise rights</h2>
			<p>You may update your account email, update or delete sites, and delete your account through the service. You may also stop publishing a site by changing its public status or deleting it.</p>
			<p>Other privacy requests can be sent to the operator of Conex through the support or contact channel provided for the service. To protect accounts and third parties, Conex may need to verify your identity before completing a request. If you believe your rights were violated, you may contact the Agencia de Proteccion de Datos de los Habitantes (Prodhab) in Costa Rica or your competent data protection authority in the European Economic Area or United Kingdom.</p>
		</section>
		<section>
			<h2>14. Changes and contact</h2>
			<p>We may update this policy as the service changes. Questions about this policy can be sent to the operator of Conex through the support or contact channel provided for the service.</p>
		</section>
	</article>
}
